    "The type check must run before the range check, and the existing out-of-range behavior and bucket boundaries must be preserved unchanged",
    "Follow TDD: add the failing regression test before the source change",
    "No new dependency for a change this small"
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    {
      "id": "AC-1",
      "description": "classify_credit_score(700.5) raises loanflow.errors.ValidationError instead of returning CreditBucket.GOOD; an integral float such as 700.0 is also rejected"
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-2",
      "description": "classify_credit_score(True) and classify_credit_score(False) raise loanflow.errors.ValidationError, since bool is an int subclass and must be explicitly excluded as Money/Percentage already do"
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-3",
      "description": "Existing behavior is preserved: integer scores still map to the same CreditBucket at every boundary (579/580/669/670/739/740), and 299/851 still raise ValidationError"
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-4",
      "description": "A regression test covering the non-int rejection exists in demo-repo/tests/unit/test_risk_bands.py and passes, and the full demo-repo unit suite remains green"
    }
